bosun uninstall --apply

bosun will make 7 changes:

  1. Restore your original status line in ~/.claude/settings.json
       Removes the bosun wrapper; your original command is put back.

  2. Remove bosun's tmux config line from ~/.tmux.conf
       - source-file -q ~/.local/share/bosun/tmux.conf

  3. Unbind C-a W, C-a a and bosun's attach hook in the running tmux

  4. Uninstall the Claude Code plugin
       claude plugin uninstall bosun@bosun
       claude plugin marketplace remove bosun

  5. Delete ~/.local/state/bosun

  6. Delete ~/.local/share/bosun

  7. Delete ~/.config/bosun

Backups of settings.json and .tmux.conf are saved before writing.
(--show-diff prints the full before and after.)

Apply? [y/N] Nothing changed.

The binary is yours to remove: rm ~/.local/bin/bosun
